diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index b677f4e..629416a 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -6,4 +6,25 @@ A small expense ledger. Entries live in a JSON file (`--data` or `$LEDGER_DATA`)
     python -m ledger list
     python -m ledger report --by month
 
+Add a monthly recurring entry with an inclusive end date:
+
+    python -m ledger add 2026-01-31 25 subscriptions "monthly plan" --repeat monthly --until 2026-04-30
+
+This produces occurrences on January 31, February 28, March 31, and April 30.
+Each month uses the original day, clamped to that month's last day (including
+February 29 in leap years). Every occurrence keeps the amount, category, and
+note. Listing is chronological, and both category and monthly reports include
+all occurrences alongside ordinary entries.
+
+Only `monthly` is supported. `--repeat monthly` requires `--until YYYY-MM-DD`,
+which must be a valid date on or after the entry's start date. `--until` requires
+`--repeat`. Invalid arguments return status 2 with a message on stderr and leave
+the data file untouched, including when it does not exist yet.
+
+Storage remains a JSON list. A recurring entry stores one record with `repeat`
+and `until` fields; occurrences are generated only for listing and reports.
+Reading never rewrites the file, and adding entries keeps existing series
+unexpanded. Ordinary entries retain their original field format, and older
+files without recurrence fields continue to load and accept additions.
+
 Tests: `python -m unittest discover -s tests`.
